## Error Debugging

### Error Boundaries

```typescript
// Add error logging to error boundary
class ErrorBoundary extends React.Component {
  componentDidCatch(error: Error, errorInfo: React.ErrorInfo) {
    console.error('[ErrorBoundary]', {
      error: error.message,
      stack: error.stack,
      componentStack: errorInfo.componentStack,
    });
    // Send to error tracking service
  }
}
```

### Error Stack Traces

- Read error stack traces carefully
- Identify source of error
- Check component hierarchy
- Verify prop types
- Check API responses

## Common Debugging Scenarios

### Component Not Rendering

```typescript
// Check if component is receiving props
console.log('[Component] Props:', props);

// Check if condition is met
console.log('[Component] Condition:', condition);

// Check if data exists
console.log('[Component] Data:', data);
```

### State Not Updating

```typescript
// Log state changes
useEffect(() => {
  console.log('[Component] State changed:', state);
}, [state]);

// Check if state setter is called
const handleUpdate = () => {
  console.log('[Component] Updating state');
  setState(newState);
};
```

### API Not Working

```typescript
// Check request configuration
console.log('[API] Request config:', {
  url: config.url,
  method: config.method,
  headers: config.headers,
  data: config.data,
});

// Check response
console.log('[API] Response:', {
  status: response.status,
  data: response.data,
});
```

